193.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">A circle marks where a</text><text x="580.0" y="205.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">flow scenario crosses the</text><text x="580.0" y="217.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">48 hour line. To the left</text><text x="580.0" y="229.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">of it, 48 hours is not</text><text x="580.0" y="241.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">long enough.</text><text x="580.0" y="265.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">Both the low and the</text><text x="580.0" y="277.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">typical flow cross inside</text><text x="580.0" y="289.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">the published range of k.</text><text x="580.0" y="301.0" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#4A555C" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" letter-spacing="0">That is the finding.</text></svg></div><figcaption><b>The sweep.</b> How long the water stays above 235 CFU/100 mL after the overflow stops, plotted against the die-off coefficient across the published range, for three real discharges over the Dundee Dam. The 48 hour rule is the red line. A circle marks where each flow